course: dictionary
lesson: 43
title: Accident: by chance, not on purpose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An accident is something that happens by chance, without anyone planning it. Often it is bad, and someone gets hurt or something gets broken. «By accident» means not on purpose.
explain: «The advice is never to go onto ice on ponds, lakes, rivers or canals.» The ice may look safe, but it can crack, so a fall through it is an accident. The sentence warns you about danger, which is a clue to what the word means.
explain: «At a self-checkout it is easy to miss something by accident.» The words «by accident» tell you the shopper did not mean to leave something unpaid. To test your meaning, swap in «on purpose». If the sentence stops making sense, the word means something that happened by chance.
fact: An accident is something that happens by chance, often causing harm or damage, like a car crash or a fall.
fact: An accident can also be anything that happens without anyone planning it.
fact: «By accident» means not on purpose.
fact: «A&E», Accident and Emergency, is for serious injuries and illnesses; in the USA it is called the ER.
fact: If someone is badly hurt in an accident, stay calm, get an adult and call the emergency number.
exercise: «At a self-checkout it is easy to miss something by accident.» What does «by accident» mean? | Right at the end of the shopping | Very quickly, in a rush | With a lot of care and planning | *Not on purpose
exercise: Which of these is an example of an accident? | *Tripping over a loose step and falling | Planning a surprise party for a friend | Reading a book quietly by the fire | Saving money to buy a new bike
exercise: From «A&E, Accident and Emergency, is for serious injuries and illnesses», find and copy one word that means harm to the body. | Accident | *injuries | Emergency | Illnesses
test: Ella says an accident is always done on purpose. Is she right? | Yes, because she is always right | Yes, every accident is planned in advance | *No, an accident happens by chance, not on purpose | Only if somebody is hurt
test: What is the best thing to do if someone is badly hurt in an accident? | *Stay calm, get an adult and call the emergency number | Wait and see if it stops hurting | Run away and hide until it is over | Do nothing, because it was only an accident
exam: Which sentence uses accident correctly? | I did it on purpose by accident. | The accident was a long, quiet book about cats. | I planned the accident for the party next week. | *I knocked the vase over by accident, and I said sorry.
